      "register_notes": "CR0/CR1 shared encoding, INTF W0C through ICR at +0x08, direct RAM not buffered update handshake. Table 26-9 and \u00a726.7 expose RAM0\u20138 and RAM13 only: remove unsupported SVD RAM9\u201312 accessors, no silicon claim about undocumented addresses.",
      "bias_scope": "Internal resistor only. BUMP=0. VLCD pins are not consumed unless used as SEG24\u201327, then MUX=1. External resistor/capacitor/pump paths require a future board circuit API.",
      "electrical": "LCD maximum waveform VLCD4 <= VDD; no source-backed contrast-to-voltage transfer or pump readiness maximum. User declares maximum board supply and panel tolerated peak drive. LSI frequency is typical only; no elapsed-time guarantee.",
      "clock_policy": "Software requests LSI through keyed SYSCTRL_CR1.LSIEN then polls enable readback and SYSCTRL_LSI.STABLE. Does not rely on LCD auto-enabling its source. Existing TRIM/WAITCYCLE and all shared control fields remain; LSI stays enabled after errors/drop. Factory accuracy tables are not claimed for the retained trim. IWDT uses separate RC10K on these parts; RTC/AUTOTRIM automatic-wakeup/clock-security users are not reconfigured.",
      "rendered_review": {
        "manual_pdf_pages": [
          551,
          554
        ],
        "findings": "L052 register-table omission of RAM9\u201312 confirmed visually; both CR1/clear tables show frame INTF RO and clear bit12 W0C. IE-independent latching is not stated, so HAL uses an owned-source interrupt binding."
      }
    },
